{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control","id":1516384,"title":"The Tradition in control","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-27T17:27:01-07:00","id":1516384,"title":"The Tradition in control","content":"This right here is a thought I had while I was discussing, if it weren't for Technocracy being an antagonist to the traditions, there's a possibility that the traditions would be at odds with each other, at least some of them would be, more by ideology than anything else, I could be wrong, but for the sake of argument let's assume that this is the case, what do you think would happen next if the traditions somehow defeated the technocracy or if one of them was a new Technocracy in fact and shaped the world to their creed, how do you think it would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:45:39-07:00","id":1516391,"title":"","content":"You might end up with something more akin to the Seers of the Throne from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>. I really don't see any one Tradition deciding to take control; as a rule, their attitude toward the Sleepers tends to be less a matter of \u201ccontrolling\u201d and more \u201cneglectful\u201d. There may be some Disparate factions that might go for a global power play; the Wu Lung spring to mind. But they'd generally need to be a <i>lot </i>more powerful than they currently are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:16:29-07:00","id":1516396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516391#post1516391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might end up with something more akin to the Seers of the Throne from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>. I really don't see any one Tradition deciding to take control; as a rule, their attitude toward the Sleepers tends to be less a matter of \u201ccontrolling\u201d and more \u201cneglectful\u201d. There may be some Disparate factions that might go for a global power play; the Wu Lung spring to mind. But they'd generally need to be a <i>lot </i>more powerful than they currently are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about a hypothetical case, if it's easier to think about, you can think about the case of one tradition getting much stronger than the others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T20:20:35-07:00","id":1516410,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the Ars Magica rpg is predicated on the idea that the Order of Hermes is the dominant magic faction and all of their ideas are more or less true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:18:08-07:00","id":1516448,"title":"","content":"I remember a discussion some time ago about an alternate history where it was an alliance of mystical groups that united Technocracy that came together to impose their paradigms on the world. I can't find it now.<br /> <br /> That's really what it would take. The Traditions as they are now would not go full Technocrat even if they won. They've spent far too long working with other, seemingly irreconcilable paradigms and practices. Instead, look for what is frightening or dystopian about what the Traditions are fighting for right now and use that as the starting point for what they would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T14:01:27-07:00","id":1516525,"title":"","content":"Akashics: you're interrupting my meditation peasant. And if &quot;food&quot; is all you care about instead of Enlightenment, then you're wasting both of our times.<br /> <br /> Chakravanti: so, you're wasting your entire life &quot;farming&quot; instead of trying to comprehend the great karmic cycle... Im sorry, but you're just stuck in your karmic wheel, so I'll have to release you, so that in your next life you may advance.<br /> <br /> Chorus: you're not pure enough, begone peasant, and rethink your actions. Starvation will help cleanse your soul.<br /> <br /> Verbena: your life is unimportant in the grand scheme of things; your death will feed countless lives. <br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers: Im sorry, but giving you food now would imbalance the spirit world. The spirits told me that this season, there's no food for your family.<br /> <br /> Virtual Adepts: get lost newbie, this area is for elite only.<br /> <br /> Etherites: who let this unneducated troglodyte into my lab? Food? Get lost peasant, Im uncovering the secrets of the cosmos, I dont have time to waste with your little men concerns.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes: who let this &quot;mundane&quot; into my chambers? Guards! Remove this peasantt from my tower!<br /> <br /> That's what &quot;Traditions in control&quot; would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:17:37-07:00","id":1516532,"title":"","content":"Exactly. As I said before, their attitude toward the Sleepers tends to be less a matter of \u201ccontrolling\u201d and more \u201cneglectful\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T15:27:37-07:00","id":1516535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516525#post1516525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what &quot;Traditions in control&quot; would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are being too pessimistic, and not cynical enough. You don\u2019t have to look for malice or disdain when callousness, blindness, or tunnel vision will explain things. <br /> <br /> Thats true for the Technocracy too. Some justify their tyranny but most don\u2019t even realize they are perpetuating it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:26:22-07:00","id":1516556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516525#post1516525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Akashics: you're interrupting my meditation peasant. And if &quot;food&quot; is all you care about instead of Enlightenment, then you're wasting both of our times.<br /> <br /> Chakravanti: so, you're wasting your entire life &quot;farming&quot; instead of trying to comprehend the great karmic cycle... Im sorry, but you're just stuck in your karmic wheel, so I'll have to release you, so that in your next life you may advance.<br /> <br /> Chorus: you're not pure enough, begone peasant, and rethink your actions. Starvation will help cleanse your soul.<br /> <br /> Verbena: your life is unimportant in the grand scheme of things; your death will feed countless lives.<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers: Im sorry, but giving you food now would imbalance the spirit world. The spirits told me that this season, there's no food for your family.<br /> <br /> Virtual Adepts: get lost newbie, this area is for elite only.<br /> <br /> Etherites: who let this unneducated troglodyte into my lab? Food? Get lost peasant, Im uncovering the secrets of the cosmos, I dont have time to waste with your little men concerns.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes: who let this &quot;mundane&quot; into my chambers? Guards! Remove this peasantt from my tower!<br /> <br /> That's what &quot;Traditions in control&quot; would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Akashic: Strangely I think that out of all of them she's really the only one who wouldn't make any major changes, to say the least, I'm not very knowledgeable about that tradition, but I think she'd keep it out and let things go naturally.<br /> <br /> Chorus: This one would have made the world &quot;unite&quot; around the &quot;One&quot; as a religious organization that controls the world openly and its most questionable actions would be done discreetly, the sleepers would know about these actions despite not knowing their full extent. How this would fit in with other religions I don't know, as this is already a discussion within the tradition itself. As for the paradox I believe it would be circumvented by faith and in theory and the other traditions would be at an extreme disadvantage because of it. By the way, probably the technology would have developed with a lot of restraint so maybe now we still have pre-war technology.<br /> <br /> Verbena: I believe that they would have stopped any advance that would have led humanity to have a great technological development which would make the paradox much weaker as a consequence, I don't know if the world would have stopped in the Middle Ages or not.<br /> <br /> Virtual Adepts: I imagine they would dominate the world through the digital network, and eventually try to make the world follow the same path, of course that would only work in first world countries. One scenario that comes to mind is that maybe they would develop something like a nutritional spread that kills hunger but has virtually no taste.<br /> <br /> SoE: Possibly the most chaotic scenario, I believe these are the ones that would try to help the most if they could, but they have so many different lines of reasoning and conflicting ideas that the world would become a mess and maybe they would blow up, or at best would become a less efficient technocracy.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes: I think the world would have evolved around the belief in magic as a science, the world would have been more elitist involving the hermetic houses, but it's possible that a good result would have come from that.<br /> <br /> So I was curious, how do you play or would you play as a member of one of the traditions? I have some ideas, but maybe they're a bit stereotyped and to take the hint, you didn't mention the Euthanatos, is there some reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:29:01-07:00","id":1516558,"title":"","content":"Magus Maximus forgot the Cult of Ecstasy. Maybe they were to busy partying to be found.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:42:34-07:00","id":1516560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516556#post1516556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was curious, how do you play or would you play as a member of one of the traditions? I have some ideas, but maybe they're a bit stereotyped and to take the hint, you didn't mention the Euthanatos, is there some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chakravanti = Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> Chakravanti is their M20 ed &quot;Politically Correct&quot; name.<br /> And by the way, I prefer the original names too (up to Rev)<br /> <br /> The only ones I forgot are the Cult of Ecstasy because well... They're forgettable. I always disliked them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as in how to play them, well my absolute favorite has always been the Etherites - mad scientists, how could anyone not love them. After that, the good ol' hermetics.<br /> <br /> I went to ChatGPT just to improve the Spirit Worlds for my games; Im feverishly designing to play shamans (outside of WoD), Im even thinking about playing a game with shamans only (Im always the ST), so Dreamspeakers, I also love 'em.<br /> <br /> I gotta say, Im a big Technocracy fanboy. They are my favorite &quot;mages&quot;. In real life I would hate them (but probably I would hate ALL Mages anyway), but in the game they are my favorites (NWO all the way baby, behold my memeticist wizard!), but I do love many traditions too.<br /> <br /> My least favorite is the Cult of Ecstasy. Im also not very fond of Euthanathoi or Akashics (all that &quot;monk class&quot; vibe is not for me). And, speaking about classes, the &quot;Cleric&quot; (Choristers) and &quot;Druid&quot; (Verbena) never got my attention on D&amp;D and neither do they do here.<br /> <br /> As for the VA... Neutral reaction.<br /> <br /> But playing as an Etherite is were I really shine. But lately I've being on a very &quot;New Age&quot; zen-feeling, thus if I had to pick one for a new table, I would go with Dreamspeakers, and lets go commune with mother nature brother","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:55:49-07:00","id":1516562,"title":"","content":"The Cult of Ecstasy... <i>Forgettable</i>? That just feels <i>wrong</i>. <br /> <br /> It's one thing to not care for playing hedonists or stoners, but CoE Revised is one of the few Ascension books I got and they're so much more. The character template had Barstool Philosophers, extreme athletes and even someone who could channel Loas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:56:13-07:00","id":1516563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516560#post1516560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chakravanti = Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> Chakravanti is their M20 ed &quot;Politically Correct&quot; name.<br /> And by the way, I prefer the original names too (up to Rev)<br /> <br /> The only ones I forgot are the Cult of Ecstasy because well... They're forgettable. I always disliked them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as in how to play them, well my absolute favorite has always been the Etherites - mad scientists, how could anyone not love them. After that, the good ol' hermetics.<br /> <br /> I went to ChatGPT just to improve the Spirit Worlds for my games; Im feverishly designing to play shamans (outside of WoD), Im even thinking about playing a game with shamans only (Im always the ST), so Dreamspeakers, I also love 'em.<br /> <br /> I gotta say, Im a big Technocracy fanboy. They are my favorite &quot;mages&quot;. In real life I would hate them (but probably I would hate ALL Mages anyway), but in the game they are my favorites (NWO all the way baby, behold my memeticist wizard!), but I do love many traditions too.<br /> <br /> My least favorite is the Cult of Ecstasy. Im also not very fond of Euthanathoi or Akashics (all that &quot;monk class&quot; vibe is not for me). And, speaking about classes, the &quot;Cleric&quot; (Choristers) and &quot;Druid&quot; (Verbena) never got my attention on D&amp;D and neither do they do here.<br /> <br /> As for the VA... Neutral reaction.<br /> <br /> But playing as an Etherite is were I really shine. But lately I've being on a very &quot;New Age&quot; zen-feeling, thus if I had to pick one for a new table, I would go with Dreamspeakers, and lets go commune with mother nature brother</div> </div> </div> </div>In case I wanted something more specific, I mean, WOD is a game where you interpret in a certain way and it also has social aspects, apart from that even traditions have internal factions within them, so how would you interpret that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:57:21-07:00","id":1516564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516558#post1516558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magus Maximus forgot the Cult of Ecstasy. Maybe they were to busy partying to be found.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or whipping each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:17:21-07:00","id":1516572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516562#post1516562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cult of Ecstasy... <i>Forgettable</i>? That just feels <i>wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to not care for playing hedonists or stoners, but CoE Revised is one of the few Ascension books I got and they're so much more. The character template had Barstool Philosophers, extreme athletes and even someone who could channel Loas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty cool but... I still dont care lol<br /> <br /> It's cool that you like 'em thou, more power to you. That's the thing about the Trads, diversity. So each to their own.<br /> <br /> I just dont like 'em. Subjective taste.<br /> <br /> Edit PS: much like I dont like Akashics (monk \ud83d\ude29) or Verbena, Choristers or Euthanathoi. The hermetics made a mistake when they invited THESE guys if you ask me... Strangely, when I said this on the last etherite symposium they called me a &quot;racist&quot;, I have no idea why... I even have a Dreamspeaker friend... And he mostly agrees with me too, althought he told me that the hermetics should kick themselves out too but hey, nobody calls him a &quot;racist&quot; for that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 06-28-2023, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:15:59-07:00","id":1516587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516572#post1516572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit PS: much like I dont like Akashics (monk \ud83d\ude29) or Verbena, Choristers or Euthanathoi. The hermetics made a mistake when they invited THESE guys if you ask me... Strangely, when I said this on the last etherite symposium they called me a &quot;racist&quot;, I have no idea why... I even have a Dreamspeaker friend... And he mostly agrees with me too, althought he told me that the hermetics should kick themselves out too but hey, nobody calls him a &quot;racist&quot; for that...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this is related, but in the transition from Rev to M20 a new faction kind of &quot;took over&quot; and that it intends to be more open-minded than the original SoE, so much so there is a text making comparisons between development academic and sexism and this change led to the change of name from Sons of Ether to Society of Ether. Anyway I haven't read their tradition book so I'm not sure, if anyone knows let me know, but it could be related to this, especially if you've talked about it online. People mix it all theses days.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:19:16-07:00","id":1516589,"title":"","content":"The upcoming <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> gets into this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:45:50-07:00","id":1516593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516587#post1516587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if this is related, but in the transition from Rev to M20 a new faction kind of &quot;took over&quot; and that it intends to be more open-minded than the original SoE, so much so there is a text making comparisons between development academic and sexism and this change led to the change of name from Sons of Ether to Society of Ether. Anyway I haven't read their tradition book so I'm not sure, if anyone knows let me know, but it could be related to this, especially if you've talked about it online. People mix it all theses days.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why M20 SUCKS.<br /> <br /> I want play with the &quot;Awaken&quot;, not with the WOKE.<br /> <br /> I absolutely want my SONS of Ether to be chauvinistic arrogant a holes. I dont want politically correct idiots forged in the fires of the PC wokeist mob. I want oligarchic Hermetics and elitist VAs and authoritarian Techies. I dont want these guys to be perfectly aligned with the lgbt+ vocabulary, nor do I want them to adopt wokeist language. That's stupid, I want them to be IMPERFECT. I want them to be HUMAN.<br /> <br /> <b>They are the freaking TRADITIONS for freaking sake!!!</b>. Traditions! Not &quot;transgressives&quot;! Traditions! <br /> <br /> I dont care 2 seconds about M20. The SONS will always continue to be THE SONS of Ether on my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T20:01:39-07:00","id":1516596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516593#post1516593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why M20 SUCKS.<br /> <br /> I want play with the &quot;Awaken&quot;, not with the WOKE.<br /> <br /> I absolutely want my SONS of Ether to be chauvinistic arrogant a holes. I dont want politically correct idiots forged in the fires of the PC wokeist mob. I want oligarchic Hermetics and elitist VAs and authoritarian Techies. I dont want these guys to be perfectly aligned with the lgbt+ vocabulary, nor do I want them to adopt wokeist language. That's stupid, I want them to be IMPERFECT. I want them to be HUMAN.<br /> <br /> <b>They are the freaking TRADITIONS for freaking sake!!!</b>. Traditions! Not &quot;transgressives&quot;! Traditions!<br /> <br /> I dont care 2 seconds about M20. The SONS will always continue to be THE SONS of Ether on my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only read the revised edition, so I have no opinion and generaly I am call then SoE so I am all good with anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T23:05:01-07:00","id":1516612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516410#post1516410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the Ars Magica rpg is predicated on the idea that the Order of Hermes is the dominant magic faction and all of their ideas are more or less true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am wandering - are there any mentions and descriptions, or at least some basic and standard attention, consideration, and respect given and shown to establishments, orders, guilds, fellowships, teams, or factions other than the Order of Hermes ?<br /> <br /> In regard to traditional and common legends, stories, portrayals, and records, there are Druids and Witches in Ireland, Wales, England, and Scotland, and also as well there are interesting and unique Bards and Spellcasters in the Scandinavia.<br /> And of course there should be Witches and Sorceresses comparable and simillar to the Verbenae in various areas and regions of Europe - for example in France, Poland, Latvia, Italy and Sicilly, Spain, Portugal, Romania and Moldavia, Estonia, and Lithuania. <br /> <br /> Seems to be that other than Order of Hermes, Ars Magica could definitely and clearly contain descriptions, details, and stories about some additional wizard, magic, occult, and mystical groups and fellowships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T23:51:08-07:00","id":1516615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516612#post1516612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wandering - are there any mentions and descriptions, or at least some basic and standard attention, consideration, and respect given and shown to establishments, orders, guilds, fellowships, teams, or factions other than the Order of Hermes ?<br /> <br /> In regard to traditional and common legends, stories, portrayals, and records, there are Druids and Witches in Ireland, Wales, England, and Scotland, and also as well there are interesting and unique Bards and Spellcasters in the Scandinavia.<br /> And of course there should be Witches and Sorceresses comparable and simillar to the Verbenae in various areas and regions of Europe - for example in France, Poland, Latvia, Italy and Sicilly, Spain, Portugal, Romania and Moldavia, Estonia, and Lithuania.<br /> <br /> Seems to be that other than Order of Hermes, Ars Magica could definitely and clearly contain descriptions, details, and stories about some additional wizard, magic, occult, and mystical groups and fellowships.</div> </div> </div> </div>To qualify No One's statement, Ars Magica has the Order as the dominant magic faction in Europe, but they're not the only magic faction in Europe, and they're not dominant outside it - for example, the Order of Suleiman holds sway in the Middle East. There are several books on the other factions in Fifth Edition (<i>Hedge Magic Revised, Rival Magic, The Cradle and the Crescent</i> for the Order of Suleiman, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T01:28:30-07:00","id":1516621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516612#post1516612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wandering - are there any mentions and descriptions, or at least some basic and standard attention, consideration, and respect given and shown to establishments, orders, guilds, fellowships, teams, or factions other than the Order of Hermes ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really an expert on Ars Magica. Most of the books I have are stuff I picked up looking for more information to mine for the Order of Hermes and for general Dark Ages geography and culture. <br /> <br /> I do know that 5th edition has a book called Rival Magic, which included four new local mystical factions that could be rivals to the Order in certain areas. They were, I think, the Amazons (based on the Greek myths and located on the island of Amazonia in the Caspian Sea), the Muspelli (Nordic Jotun worshipers), the sorcerers of Soqotra (isolationists living on an island in the Arabian Sea), and the Augustan Brotherhood (a secret society of court wizards who practice their own style of Roman inherited magic and have the ultimate aim of trying to reform the old Roman Empire). <br /> If you wanted to, you could certainly try to tie said groups to the Sisterhood of Hipolita, Nordic Infernalists/Nephandi, Taftini or Ahl i Batin, and the proto-Order of Reason. <br /> <br /> The 4th edition book Ultima Thule: Mythic Scandinavia goes into detail about Scandinavian and Norse wizards, including some stuff about Finnish practices. <br /> <br /> The 4th edition book Kabballah: Mythic Judaism covers various forms of Jewish mysticism, especially in Iberia. <br /> <br /> The 4th edition book The Dragon &amp; The Bear covers Russia and talks about Slavic, Siberian, and Mongol magic. <br /> <br /> There are four books about the Islamic world. 4th edition's Blood &amp; Sand (the Levant), and 5th edition's Between Sand and Sea (North Africa), Lands of the Nile (Egypt, Nubia, and Ethiopia), and The Cradle and The Crescent (Mesopotamia and Persia). Each talks about certain mystical traditions native to their regions. <br /> <br /> And the 5th edition book The Contested Isle covers Ireland, and has a little bit of stuff about druids and other Irish mythic traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T01:38:55-07:00","id":1516622,"title":"","content":"If you want a possible idea for an Etherite dominated world/timeline, GURPS Alternate Earths 1 has the world of Gernsback, which is essentially golden age sci fi predicated on Tesla created super science. <br /> <br /> The second volume includes two worlds dominated by a global Islamic califate and the Ming dynasty of China if you want ideas for possible Batini and Wu Lung dominated realities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T06:06:11-07:00","id":1516637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control#post1516384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This right here is a thought I had while I was discussing, if it weren't for Technocracy being an antagonist to the traditions, there's a possibility that the traditions would be at odds with each other, at least some of them would be, more by ideology than anything else, I could be wrong, but for the sake of argument let's assume that this is the case, what do you think would happen next if the traditions somehow defeated the technocracy or if one of them was a new Technocracy in fact and shaped the world to their creed, how do you think it would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean if the Technocracy never existed? If yes, then I would say that the antagonists would probably be the Nehandi. <br /> <br /> A Tradition would never be the *antagonist* because they are on the same side. There would not be an Ascension War. There could be small territory wars, if the Traditions were as cocky as they were back then (before the Technocracy screwing them in the original setting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T06:09:23-07:00","id":1516638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516593#post1516593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why M20 SUCKS.<br /> <br /> I want play with the &quot;Awaken&quot;, not with the WOKE.<br /> <br /> I absolutely want my SONS of Ether to be chauvinistic arrogant a holes. I dont want politically correct idiots forged in the fires of the PC wokeist mob. I want oligarchic Hermetics and elitist VAs and authoritarian Techies. I dont want these guys to be perfectly aligned with the lgbt+ vocabulary, nor do I want them to adopt wokeist language. That's stupid, I want them to be IMPERFECT. I want them to be HUMAN.<br /> <br /> <b>They are the freaking TRADITIONS for freaking sake!!!</b>. Traditions! Not &quot;transgressives&quot;! Traditions!<br /> <br /> I dont care 2 seconds about M20. The SONS will always continue to be THE SONS of Ether on my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU!!! The book has about 700 pages and the motherfucker spends expensive words to talk about neutral pronomes and sexuality, WHAT THE FUCK?? I dont want fucking political agenda in a RPG game. That's really ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Although, I still consider M20 a great book. Just completely ignore any wokism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T07:32:48-07:00","id":1516646,"title":"","content":"The problem with Wokeism, as opposed to just plain good manners, is that, like Leninism and Fascism, it's built on the Terror/Virtue ideology. The view that you can coherse people into being virtuous. When Robbespierre tried it in France it led to the Emperor Napoleon. In Russia the same idea lead to Plutocratic Oligarchy. Hitler totally ruined Germany. Mao ultimately made China a Plutocratic Oligarchy as well and stripped the Chinese people of their culture into the bargain. <br /> <br /> Wokeism is a play for social status that intends to grind society into submission. It uses shaming and shunning instead of death camps, but Wokeism is solely about power without moral responsibility. <br /> <br /> That's why I think Wokeism is perfect for the Technocracy. Wokeism is a whip and a scalpel to shape society into whatever form the powerful desire with proclaiming itself the voice of the weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T07:38:12-07:00","id":1516647,"title":"","content":"This might just be me, but I feel that the Batini would be the ones to win out in the end, mainly due to how after leaving the Traditions they not only incited conflict between the Technocracy and the Taftani, but with aid from the Web of Faith were able to force the Technocratic Union into leaving the Middle East, something I dont believe any other Tradition was able to replicate. What I feel they really have going for them however, is their focus and understanding of subtle power, something which I feel the other traditions lack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T08:22:00-07:00","id":1516653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516646#post1516646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I think Wokeism is perfect for the Technocracy. Wokeism is a whip and a scalpel to shape society into whatever form the powerful desire with proclaiming itself the voice of the weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's an argument to be made about the flipside. If you control enough public opinion through media, you can easily whip up the non-issue of people wanting to live as their chosen identity into an extremist agenda, to the point where a five sentence text-box about gender neutral pronouns in a 700 page book is perceived as offensive or that people draw comparisons with the <i>Third Reich</i>. I would argue that the concept of a fluid Identity (as in, the Magick term) is more threatening to the Technocracy's Consensus as opposed to a useful vehicle for control, and they would rather launch a disinformation campaign.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">I don't really feel like discussing politics with that many exclamations marks and capital letters already flung around, even if it's veiled as a game discussion. So that's my two cents and I'm out.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T08:33:51-07:00","id":1516655,"title":"","content":"I honestly didn't expect to start a discussion like that, I swear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T10:09:31-07:00","id":1516668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516647#post1516647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might just be me, but I feel that the Batini would be the ones to win out in the end, mainly due to how after leaving the Traditions they not only incited conflict between the Technocracy and the Taftani, but with aid from the Web of Faith were able to force the Technocratic Union into leaving the Middle East, something I dont believe any other Tradition was able to replicate. What I feel they really have going for them however, is their focus and understanding of subtle power, something which I feel the other traditions lack.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the Batini were first fully introduced in the 1st edition Book of Shadows players guide, there was a lot of implications that they were somehow the secret masterminds behind everything involving the creation of the Council of Nine and even some of the Traditions themselves. I was never much of a fan of this personally just because I feel it undermines the other Traditions having their own agency and makes them (and people playing characters from them) feel less important. YMMV.<br /> But it does offer ideas about how they might run things if in charge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T11:22:30-07:00","id":1516674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516668#post1516668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When the Batini were first fully introduced in the 1st edition Book of Shadows players guide, there was a lot of implications that they were somehow the secret masterminds behind everything involving the creation of the Council of Nine and even some of the Traditions themselves. I was never much of a fan of this personally just because I feel it undermines the other Traditions having their own agency and makes them (and people playing characters from them) feel less important. YMMV.<br /> But it does offer ideas about how they might run things if in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading some of the lore books, like the Tradition books, it makes sense to me that the Batini were the ones behind it. A majority of the Traditions cannot really be called organizations and realistically would either be warring with each other or simply surviving on the fringes of society, so it makes sense that an organization of mages with a specialty in subtlety and a core doctrine of unity would be the one that brings them together.<br /> <br /> Even then, I still find it hard to believe that the traditions are capable of opposing the Technocratic union in any meaningful way. To me, Mage the Ascension feels like a better version of the Camarilla vs a worse version of the Sabbat. I am actually surprised that the Technocracy still cares about the Traditions. If they are making a nuisance of themselves, sure wipe them out. But if they're just minding their own businesses, why care? Their backs are broken, there really isn't anything they can do to win, or even hurt the union.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T04:25:52-07:00","id":1516756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516674#post1516674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, I still find it hard to believe that the traditions are capable of opposing the Technocratic union in any meaningful way. To me, Mage the Ascension feels like a better version of the Camarilla vs a worse version of the Sabbat. I am actually surprised that the Technocracy still cares about the Traditions. If they are making a nuisance of themselves, sure wipe them out. But if they're just minding their own businesses, why care? Their backs are broken, there really isn't anything they can do to win, or even hurt the union.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the inherent aspects of authoritarianism is that any form of dissent, no matter how small, is seen as a threat. Essentially, power itself - whatever ends it claims to be aiming for, be they &quot;good&quot; or &quot;bad&quot; - becomes a sort of religious dogma and any disagreement a form of heresy that must be stamped out lest it inspire others. This is, unfortunately, one of the basics of human nature that most utopian movements - the Union included - tend to ignore.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T04:34:01-07:00","id":1516758,"title":"","content":"A Dreamspeaker dominated world would be an openly animist one. I could swear I have seen some sort of fictional representation of this but can't recall where. But it would incorporate a lot of the Shinto influence you see in certain anime (as well as traditional shamanism that crops up occasionally in K-drama), as well as some urban fantasy works, and horror like The Exorcist, Fallen, and Evil Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T04:46:28-07:00","id":1516759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516638#post1516638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THANK YOU!!! The book has about 700 pages and the motherfucker spends expensive words to talk about neutral pronomes and sexuality, WHAT THE FUCK?? I dont want fucking political agenda in a RPG game. That's really ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Although, I still consider M20 a great book. Just completely ignore any wokism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Akashic BROTHERHOOD. A 3000 years old TRADITION now all of a sudden wants to be &quot;gender neutral&quot;? Hell no!<br /> <br /> Let them and the hermetics and the choristers and the victorian era etherites be openly bigots! Let them be chauvinists!<br /> <br /> I'd have no problem with the book openly criticizing these groups, even under wokeist terms, but not having those (again) TRADITIONS suddenly decide to &quot;ok, it's [current] year now guys&quot;. Hell no!<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry my dear akashic &quot;sister&quot;, but we gotta follow tradition. If you want &quot;equal rights&quot;, go seek them with the Technocracy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T05:33:04-07:00","id":1516760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516653#post1516653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's an argument to be made about the flipside. If you control enough public opinion through media, you can easily whip up the non-issue of people wanting to live as their chosen identity into an extremist agenda, to the point where a five sentence text-box about gender neutral pronouns in a 700 page book is perceived as offensive or that people draw comparisons with the <i>Third Reich</i>. I would argue that the concept of a fluid Identity (as in, the Magick term) is more threatening to the Technocracy's Consensus as opposed to a useful vehicle for control, and they would rather launch a disinformation campaign.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">I don't really feel like discussing politics with that many exclamations marks and capital letters already flung around, even if it's veiled as a game discussion. So that's my two cents and I'm out.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that this &quot;non-issue&quot; have eerily similarities to Mao's Cultural Revolution. <br /> <br /> The problem isnt about the (indeed) non issue of people wanting to live as they please - heck, more than just being a &quot;non issue&quot;, to me it is a HUGE issue, since individual choice is the cornerstone of a free society, thus people being allowed to live as they please is paramount to live free from tyranny.<br /> <br /> The problem is the weaponization of virtue by the use of societal shaming. That's what Mao's Cultural Revolution did. And funnily enough, &quot;wokeism&quot; weaponizes the virtue of &quot;freedom&quot; to institute tyranny.<br /> <br /> Also, I was not &quot;offended&quot; by &quot;people wishing to express their identities&quot; - but hey, nice subconscious shaming tactic you got there pal. Maybe you cant notice it, but that's pretty Maoist totalitarian of you.<br /> <br /> No, what Im &quot;offended&quot; at is the intellectual silliness (to be gentle) that groups who have centuries or even millenia old of TRADITIONS and that pretty much HATE the modern world - and that for quite some margin are at least a bit of reactionaries - that those guys would want to adhere to the &quot;current thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> What &quot;offends&quot; me is that the World of freaking DARKNESS gets turned into the &quot;World of Inclusive Unicorns&quot;. A world upon which EVERYBODY is defined by being 50 shades of jerk suddenly everybody is worried about not hurting feelings. Sure, the guy makes human experimentation, but at least he respects pronouns...<br /> <br /> Give me a break. WoD was supposed to be exactly a criticism of the worse of society. So criticize it! Depict the most chauvinistic despicable behavior of the Traditions; show how the mega corporations controlled by the Syndicate and governments controlled by the NWO use virtue signalling what they themselves dont care about any of it, but use it as a tool for control.<br /> <br /> You know, use that as a form of CRITICISM of society. You would get a lot more sympathy towards the - yes, totally legitimate cause of people that want to live their lives as they please in peace - by having Euthanathoi viciously attacking trans people, or having Progenitors doing gruesome experiments with unwilling human subjects to force a sex change on them. That horrific view of such extremes would have a greater impact on showing the worthiness of the cause than changing the name of the Etherites to &quot;Society of Ether&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heck, design an Etherite &quot;Daughter&quot; fighting the good fight against the chauvinistc views of the elders of her own Tradition; that would be a much better game than &quot;Traditions are the good progressive guys, Tech are the evil reactionaires&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T05:44:09-07:00","id":1516762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516674#post1516674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After reading some of the lore books, like the Tradition books, it makes sense to me that the Batini were the ones behind it. A majority of the Traditions cannot really be called organizations and realistically would either be warring with each other or simply surviving on the fringes of society, so it makes sense that an organization of mages with a specialty in subtlety and a core doctrine of unity would be the one that brings them together.<br /> <br /> Even then, I still find it hard to believe that the traditions are capable of opposing the Technocratic union in any meaningful way. To me, Mage the Ascension feels like a better version of the Camarilla vs a worse version of the Sabbat. I am actually surprised that the Technocracy still cares about the Traditions. If they are making a nuisance of themselves, sure wipe them out. But if they're just minding their own businesses, why care? Their backs are broken, there really isn't anything they can do to win, or even hurt the union.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the premisse on Rev ed. The Traditions lost, and just try to survive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T05:51:54-07:00","id":1516764,"title":"","content":"If we're looking at the stated values of the Traditions, then read the Order of Hermes tradbook. The goal of the Order is a utopian society where everyone has access to all the mysteries and knowledge and the power to control their own lives. Basically, this is an anarchist society. <br /> <br /> In a world run by the Order people would focus alot more on education and skill development. And ordinary people would be charting their own courses more often. <br /> <br /> Many of the other Trads do have political ideologies. The Virtual Adepts strongly favor democracy and egalitarianism. It is in their book. This argument needs more source references. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T07:56:45-07:00","id":1516781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516762#post1516762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the premisse on Rev ed. The Traditions lost, and just try to survive</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasnt there mention of how the Traditions are still fighting back? But instead of combat, they are trying to spread their message to one community at a time, like its something, but I wouldnt expect to get too much sucess out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 06-30-2023, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T08:46:47-07:00","id":1516789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516781#post1516781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasnt there mention of how the Traditions are still fighting back? But instead of combat, they are trying to spread their message to one community at a time, like its something, but I wouldnt expect to get too much sucess out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Rev they became much more descentralized, their main strongholds at Horizon and Doissetep destroyed, the Avatar Storm... It was a mess, connected with the at the time disastrous (pun intended) &quot;end of the world&quot;. So all of their organizational structures were in shambles.<br /> <br /> I... Didnt like that metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}