name, I mean, they are still Assamites.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T16:58:54-07:00","id":1516837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516835#post1516835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the case of the worst Ministry that I even find acceptable, because, as far as I know, the cult of Set is not limited to snakes, having members of other clans, even if these are rarer, so in my view, followers of Set would be a faction and Ministry the clan. In the case of the Hecata, I only call them by name.<br /> <br /> Now Banu Haqim, from what I understand are the members of the Assamites who don't follow Haqim's dogmas/teachings, it makes sense, but I don't understand what the problem is with that name, I mean, they are still Assamites.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier, I used the example that came off the top of my head. I had assumed that, since renaming the SoE the Society, instead of the Sons, of Ether was such a oppressive capitulation to &quot;the woke mob,&quot; then somebody, somewhere, must have had a similar problem with the renaming of the Assamite Clan. It was an assumption made on bad information, and I apologize. <br /> <br /> Never let it be said that Mao Tse Tsung of 2023 refused to acknowledge his mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T20:30:19-07:00","id":1516856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516824#post1516824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone, please take a moment of silence for the latest victims of &quot;the PC woke mob.&quot; <a href=\"https://youtu.be/PfabKcoGFmE?t=53\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/PfabKcoGFmE?t=53</a><br /> <br /> <i>No one </i>is coming to anyone's house and forcing them to call the SoE &quot;the Society&quot; instead of &quot;the Sons.&quot; Or to call the Assamites the Banu Haquim, or the Cult of Ecstasy the Sahajiya. People may not realize it, but they are perfectly free to play the setting as full of elitist, anachronistic dinosaurs as you desire. In fact, I encourage them all to let <i>all</i> their red flags fly, <i>including</i> using woke as an insult. They're only doing everyone a favor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is still pretty fucking ridiculous what the book tries to do changing the name of Traditions just to be woke. And yes, woke is a negative adjective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T02:04:47-07:00","id":1516870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516856#post1516856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is still pretty fucking ridiculous what the book tries to do changing the name of Traditions just to be woke. And yes, woke is a negative adjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the guy still wonders why &quot;woke&quot; is an insult.<br /> <br /> Maybe it is because those woke lunatics (including this very Father Enoch above) are all a bunch of little totalitarian tyrants.<br /> <br /> Their virtue signalling may have worked in China, Soviet Union and Nazi Germany, but it wont work in the free democratic world because we have people ready to stand and fight for freedom and against their tyranny.<br /> <br /> The sad part is that those &quot;better than thou&quot; fools truly believe themselves to be the heroes of their own stories... They believe they are the upholders of justice, when they are just exactly like the Gestapo or the Stasi and KGB.<br /> <br /> But the nazis and soviets also believed themselves to be the heroes. That's the sad part of those many little tyrants: they cant perceive their own monstrosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T04:36:14-07:00","id":1516877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516856#post1516856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is still pretty fucking ridiculous what the book tries to do changing the name of Traditions just to be woke. And yes, woke is a negative adjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of those changes were simply that they knew more now. They've been working with the backgrounds of these groups for thirty years in some cases. Over that time you learn new things. I remember a Sci Fi/Arthurian crossover I did with Arthur returning in a post-apocalyptic Britain. By the time I finished the campaign some of the names and setting embarrassed me because of works on both British history and Arthurian literature I read while running the campaign. I saw the earlier stuff as shoddy, my players were having a blast. <br /> <br /> Let's not attribute what's probably just writers polishing their text to the arrogance of Woke.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T11:56:53-07:00","id":1516903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516877#post1516877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think some of those changes were simply that they knew more now. They've been working with the backgrounds of these groups for thirty years in some cases. Over that time you learn new things. I remember a Sci Fi/Arthurian crossover I did with Arthur returning in a post-apocalyptic Britain. By the time I finished the campaign some of the names and setting embarrassed me because of works on both British history and Arthurian literature I read while running the campaign. I saw the earlier stuff as shoddy, my players were having a blast.<br /> <br /> Let's not attribute what's probably just writers polishing their text to the arrogance of Woke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are they? The authors or the tradition?<br /> The authors are ridiculous woke morons, you can know that as a fact by the amount of space they spent on the 20th books to talk about trans and pronouns.<br /> <br /> If you meant the Traditions, why would several millenia old, cocky demigods change their fucking NAME? Just so kids this days feel good? Fuck this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T12:06:41-07:00","id":1516904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516903#post1516903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who are they? The authors or the tradition?<br /> The authors are ridiculous woke morons, you can know that as a fact by the amount of space they spent on the 20th books to talk about trans and pronouns.<br /> <br /> If you meant the Traditions, why would several millenia old, cocky demigods change their fucking NAME? Just so kids this days feel good? Fuck this.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much space they used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T13:15:43-07:00","id":1516909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516903#post1516903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you meant the Traditions, why would several millenia old, cocky demigods change their fucking NAME? Just so kids this days feel good? Fuck this.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the authors simply discovered they hadn't done a very good job in coming up with appropriate names? As in my Arthurian example, increased knowledge of what you're trying to represent leads to retrocons. <br /> <br /> Take the Hollow Ones, they simply started out Goth baby witches. As the authors worked with them, often taking major criticism from the fans, they kept changing them until they found something good.<br /> <br /> I like the present Iteration of the Hollow Ones. Romantic Rebels have so many story hooks available. And pointing out how nihilistic Romantic Rebellion can become hardly fits a narrowly Woke worldview. <br /> <br /> The authors have shown self awareness from time to time. The Woke almost never do. In fact I can't remember one time a Woke type has shown self awareness in my presence. But I'm sure some of them are self aware anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T13:35:27-07:00","id":1516911,"title":"","content":"\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44\ud83d\ude44","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T13:49:06-07:00","id":1516912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516909#post1516909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if the authors simply discovered they hadn't done a very good job in coming up with appropriate names? As in my Arthurian example, increased knowledge of what you're trying to represent leads to retrocons.<br /> <br /> Take the Hollow Ones, they simply started out Goth baby witches. As the authors worked with them, often taking major criticism from the fans, they kept changing them until they found something good.<br /> <br /> I like the present Iteration of the Hollow Ones. Romantic Rebels have so many story hooks available. And pointing out how nihilistic Romantic Rebellion can become hardly fits a narrowly Woke worldview.<br /> <br /> The authors have shown self awareness from time to time. The Woke almost never do. In fact I can't remember one time a Woke type has shown self awareness in my presence. But I'm sure some of them are self aware anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but one thing I've seen happen a few times is when a given &quot;ideology&quot; has gone too far and caused some kind of controversy that you can't ignore, the groups in question can only place the blame on a small portion, that said, this label of woke can be used that way too, and yes I believe there can be a woke with self awareness, but I recommend you think twice before considering it as you could be spreading a dangerous thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T13:50:37-07:00","id":1516913,"title":"","content":"I swear, I didn't expect the conversation to get to this point. Holy Molly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T16:37:00-07:00","id":1516925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516909#post1516909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if the authors simply discovered they hadn't done a very good job in coming up with appropriate names? As in my Arthurian example, increased knowledge of what you're trying to represent leads to retrocons.<br /> <br /> Take the Hollow Ones, they simply started out Goth baby witches. As the authors worked with them, often taking major criticism from the fans, they kept changing them until they found something good.<br /> <br /> I like the present Iteration of the Hollow Ones. Romantic Rebels have so many story hooks available. And pointing out how nihilistic Romantic Rebellion can become hardly fits a narrowly Woke worldview.<br /> <br /> The authors have shown self awareness from time to time. The Woke almost never do. In fact I can't remember one time a Woke type has shown self awareness in my presence. But I'm sure some of them are self aware anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I truly wouldnt even mind for the writers wokeism. Honestly I wouldnt. If it was made cleaverly.<br /> <br /> What I do mind is stupidity. I can only imagine a 500 years Master adressing 20 something years old disciples by their &quot;preferred pronous&quot; instead of cursing the stupid kid into Oblivion (in a very literal way).<br /> <br /> That's completely stupid beyond any reasonable measures.<br /> <br /> Instead, they would have a much better approach towards both taking a criticism about certain aspects of society that they view as problematic (like chauvinism for example) and into spreading their message.<br /> <br /> Calling the SoE as &quot;Society of Ether&quot; is just the typical virtue signalling of the wokeists - like Hitler, Stalin, Mao and mister passive-agressive &quot;Father Enoch&quot; above with his sad shaming tactics - and acomplishes nothing.<br /> <br /> Those changes were NOT born out of some sense of growth, they are just empty rhetoric to show what good members of the wokeist cult they are. That's all. It's despicable virtue signalling - just like the 2 boys in this very post that got all triggered and filled with FAKE INDIGNATION for me pointing this out and rushed to point out how Im showing my &quot;red flags&quot;, like the good Maoist totalitarian comrades that they are.<br /> <br /> Again, the social criticism is very valid; are women rated as second class citizens by the Etherites and the Akashics? Good. That's great. THAT'S the criticism. Are those guys going to change? No, why would them, they are the freaking TRADITIONS, they havent change for CENTURIES.<br /> <br /> So, that's how you give nuance... Yeah, lets fight against technocratic oppression... Meanwhile we turn a blind eye towards traditions chauvinistic tendencies like the good hipocrites we are...<br /> <br /> That's how you breed nuance, that's how you introduce criticism. That's how you point out at what you perceive as wrong in the REAL world.<br /> <br /> Not moronically turning groups of reactionaires that would want to turn the clocks back to the medieval age into the new pro gay activists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-01-2023, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T20:26:32-07:00","id":1516942,"title":"","content":"Hey people that want to scream about Wokeism you want to take that to a thread dedicated to talking about that rather than cluttering up this thread with it since that isn't what this thread is suppose to be about.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516913#post1516913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear, I didn't expect the conversation to get to this point. Holy Molly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry. We don't blame you. I've seen this nonsense pop up in all manner of threads plenty of times before. If it's one thing I've noticed about these BS culture warriors it's that they like to butt into other people's conversations to endlessly rant about the same culture war BS at the drop of a hat that they will drop themselves.<br /> <br /> Anyway on to the actual topic, the issue with the Traditions winning the Ascension War is how that victory would affect them. Remember, the Order of Reason didn't start off as the modern Technocracy. It had noble intentions in the beginning and lost it's way over time due to a number of factors. One of which being their growing power and dominance.<br /> <br /> Or for that matter the alternate future where Heylel Teomim of the First Cabal managed to bring the Order and the Traditions together only for it to create an even worse than the worst of the modern Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Or the Rev VE CB mentioning an alternate Earth when the Traditions won and became their own brand of tyranny.<br /> <br /> Or how the Craftmasons and OoR didn't just come into existence in a vacuum but as a response to the actions of other Mages at the time.<br /> <br /> Which has long indicated to me that whoever came out on top of the Ascension War would ultimately be corrupted by that victory and the power they would hold over the world because at the end of the day, Willworkers regardless of their Beliefs are still Human and prone to the same flaws. Now a world dominated by the Traditions wouldn't be the same as one dominated by the Technocracy. For starters, it would be unlikely that the VA and SoE would have jumped ship. Which combined with the nature of the other Traditions would likely mean that technology and science wouldn't be at the present state it's in while things like Faith and Mysticism would be much more dominant or rather still dominant. And it's likely through that this iteration of the Traditions would influence and control the Sleepers. <br /> <br /> Also possibly some Bygones still existing on Earth which probably isn't a good thing for the Sleepers.<br /> <br /> As for how the Traditions of this world would treat the Sleepers, it's harder to say. Best case scenario, negligent indifference where they don't care about the Sleepers one way or the other and only really help them if it benefits them while the worst case is abusive tyranny where they are the secret masters of the world and the Sleepers are their pawns and playthings.<br /> <br /> In general, the world would probably resemble something of a worse version of Horizon where the non-Awakened majority are very much second class citizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T04:16:36-07:00","id":1516962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516925#post1516925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I truly wouldnt even mind for the writers wokeism. Honestly I wouldnt. If it was made cleaverly.<br /> <br /> What I do mind is stupidity. I can only imagine a 500 years Master adressing 20 something years old disciples by their &quot;preferred pronous&quot; instead of cursing the stupid kid into Oblivion (in a very literal way).</div> </div> </div> </div>And get in massive real trouble for being a fool wasting vital resources. Ancient masters are often described as jerks but the trads do try to reign that in with mixed results.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Calling the SoE as &quot;Society of Ether&quot; is just the typical virtue signalling of the wokeists - like Hitler, Stalin, Mao and mister passive-agressive &quot;Father Enoch&quot; above with his sad shaming tactics - and acomplishes nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, the social criticism is very valid; are women rated as second class citizens by the Etherites and the Akashics? Good. That's great. THAT'S the criticism. Are those guys going to change? No, why would them, they are the freaking TRADITIONS, they havent change for CENTURIES. </div> </div> </div>One of the themes of the 20th anniversary edition is the evolution of tradition. Real Traditions are changing all the time. Traditions modify change and ground it, but totally static traditions die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> So, that's how you give nuance... Yeah, lets fight against technocratic oppression... Meanwhile we turn a blind eye towards traditions chauvinistic tendencies like the good hipocrites we are...<br /> <br /> That's how you breed nuance, that's how you introduce criticism. That's how you point out at what you perceive as wrong in the REAL world.<br /> <br /> Not moronically turning groups of reactionaires that would want to turn the clocks back to the medieval age into the new pro gay activists </div> </div> </div>There are fools and louts everywhere. And, if you look up the thread, I also despise Wokeism. But some of the changes you denounce are more issues of correcting old slip ups. Example, according to both <b>Ars Magica </b>and older editions of <b>Mage: the Ascension, </b>the Heremetics have had women as rough equals and power players in their ranks since before the time of King Arthur! They'd be aware of gender politics. The name changes for several trads represent improved knowledge of the languages involved and evolving ideas of where the group came from.<br /> <br /> Now, did the authors of the new edition display a certain desperate fear of Wokeism and a desperate need to signal that they conformed to Woke? Yes! Many of their fan bases are brutally woke. If you think Mage is too woke, try the Scion boards. But beware the Gatekeepers, and I refer to the self appointed Gatekeepers.<br /> <br /> Did they waste space in and already huge book. Yes! Did it destroy the game? Not yet.<br /> <br /> Your basic criticism is valid. But the authors aren't commissars nor gauleiters, they're just terrified of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-02-2023, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T14:36:19-07:00","id":1517000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516942#post1516942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey people that want to scream about Wokeism you want to take that to a thread dedicated to talking about that rather than cluttering up this thread with it since that isn't what this thread is suppose to be about.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Don't worry. We don't blame you. I've seen this nonsense pop up in all manner of threads plenty of times before. If it's one thing I've noticed about these BS culture warriors it's that they like to butt into other people's conversations to endlessly rant about the same culture war BS at the drop of a hat that they will drop themselves.<br /> <br /> Anyway on to the actual topic, the issue with the Traditions winning the Ascension War is how that victory would affect them. Remember, the Order of Reason didn't start off as the modern Technocracy. It had noble intentions in the beginning and lost it's way over time due to a number of factors. One of which being their growing power and dominance.<br /> <br /> Or for that matter the alternate future where Heylel Teomim of the First Cabal managed to bring the Order and the Traditions together only for it to create an even worse than the worst of the modern Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Or the Rev VE CB mentioning an alternate Earth when the Traditions won and became their own brand of tyranny.<br /> <br /> Or how the Craftmasons and OoR didn't just come into existence in a vacuum but as a response to the actions of other Mages at the time.<br /> <br /> Which has long indicated to me that whoever came out on top of the Ascension War would ultimately be corrupted by that victory and the power they would hold over the world because at the end of the day, Willworkers regardless of their Beliefs are still Human and prone to the same flaws. Now a world dominated by the Traditions wouldn't be the same as one dominated by the Technocracy. For starters, it would be unlikely that the VA and SoE would have jumped ship. Which combined with the nature of the other Traditions would likely mean that technology and science wouldn't be at the present state it's in while things like Faith and Mysticism would be much more dominant or rather still dominant. And it's likely through that this iteration of the Traditions would influence and control the Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Also possibly some Bygones still existing on Earth which probably isn't a good thing for the Sleepers.<br /> <br /> As for how the Traditions of this world would treat the Sleepers, it's harder to say. Best case scenario, negligent indifference where they don't care about the Sleepers one way or the other and only really help them if it benefits them while the worst case is abusive tyranny where they are the secret masters of the world and the Sleepers are their pawns and playthings.<br /> <br /> In general, the world would probably resemble something of a worse version of Horizon where the non-Awakened majority are very much second class citizens.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anybody can read &quot;The Cabal&quot;, which is a setting for Gurps 3e, it's basically the Order of Hermes as the rulers of the world (more than just &quot;basically&quot;. It is the OoH totally in control). And in this setting, they are like a whole new level of jerks, they still keep magic and the supernatural hidden from the &quot;mundanes&quot; because screw the masses, and the only purpose of this secret group, &quot;The Cabal&quot;, is to protect themselves. Oh, and in the setting they accept vampires, werewolves, even some weirder things (not Djinns thou, since the Cabal has waged a centuries old war against Djinns, almost driving them completely back to their plane).<br /> <br /> Just like the Technocracy strives to erradicate the Supernatural, the Cabal on the other hand strives to achieve a total monopoly over it. The Cabal thus seeks to destroy any other supernatural groups that are unaffiliated.<br /> <br /> And, while the Technocracy actually has some noble intents and they actually care about the masses well being, the Cabal truly dont give half a fuck about the &quot;mundanes&quot;. The Cabal wont even blink before crushing or using the &quot;mundanes&quot; for their own selfish devices.<br /> <br /> That's one of the examples of what a world without the Technocracy could be like. It could be better, but it could also be far, far worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T19:56:35-07:00","id":1517132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516909#post1516909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if the authors simply discovered they hadn't done a very good job in coming up with appropriate names? As in my Arthurian example, increased knowledge of what you're trying to represent leads to retrocons.<br /> <br /> Take the Hollow Ones, they simply started out Goth baby witches. As the authors worked with them, often taking major criticism from the fans, they kept changing them until they found something good.<br /> <br /> I like the present Iteration of the Hollow Ones. Romantic Rebels have so many story hooks available. And pointing out how nihilistic Romantic Rebellion can become hardly fits a narrowly Woke worldview.<br /> <br /> The authors have shown self awareness from time to time. The Woke almost never do. In fact I can't remember one time a Woke type has shown self awareness in my presence. But I'm sure some of them are self aware anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we all know that wasn't the case. Of course they should improve Traditions, but pushing a real world agenda that is undoubtedly killing all current media and entertainement, and even worse, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> put quite well, doing that in a pretty imbecile way, isn't good.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> They have spent pages and boxes in both M20 and hdydt. Probably every 20th mage book has this crap and for a book with 700+ pages, you should count every word very carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T21:33:14-07:00","id":1517194,"title":"","content":"A Thanatoic dominated world would be potentially interesting, at least from a story perspective. Everyone is perpetually reincarnating as they slowly work their way toward their potential fated destiny. And the biggest obstacle to doing that is the personal guilt, pain, and other karmic damage one might build up during their lifetime, which will weigh them down in their next incarnation, taking them that much further from their destiny. So the upper ranks of society all around the globe are going to be a class of psychopomps whose sacred duty is to help guide others through any existing trauma so that they can continue to advance. I'm not sure how good of an RPG setting you can make out of that, but it would certainly offer an interesting setting for fiction. Stuff in the vein of Quantum Leap (at least the original; I've not seen any of the remake), the K-drama Tomorrow (about a group tasked by Heaven to prevent suicides), or maybe Person of Interest (just with fate magic instead of super computers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T15:59:50-07:00","id":1517233,"title":"","content":"Something that might be interesting and would fit pretty well with the meta ideas of Mage as a game would be to include these realms of Tradition-Victory as Horizon Realms or what have you in the Umbra which characters could visit and explore possibilities of what a victory in the Ascension War might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T18:25:53-07:00","id":1517237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1517233#post1517233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that might be interesting and would fit pretty well with the meta ideas of Mage as a game would be to include these realms of Tradition-Victory as Horizon Realms or what have you in the Umbra which characters could visit and explore possibilities of what a victory in the Ascension War might look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those would make for interesting Astral realms I think. Although some Etherites might claim the Gernsback Continuum is their victory realm, and a lot of Virtual Adepts arguing if their realm would be any different from the Digital Web or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T19:06:21-07:00","id":1517238,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be a prelude to one of the apocalipse scenarios?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-08T02:12:10-07:00","id":1517459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516621#post1516621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not really an expert on Ars Magica. Most of the books I have are stuff I picked up looking for more information to mine for the Order of Hermes and for general Dark Ages geography and culture.<br /> <br /> I do know that 5th edition has a book called Rival Magic, which included four new local mystical factions that could be rivals to the Order in certain areas. They were, I think, the Amazons (based on the Greek myths and located on the island of Amazonia in the Caspian Sea), the Muspelli (Nordic Jotun worshipers), the sorcerers of Soqotra (isolationists living on an island in the Arabian Sea), and the Augustan Brotherhood (a secret society of court wizards who practice their own style of Roman inherited magic and have the ultimate aim of trying to reform the old Roman Empire).<br /> If you wanted to, you could certainly try to tie said groups to the Sisterhood of Hipolita, Nordic Infernalists/Nephandi, Taftini or Ahl i Batin, and the proto-Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> The 4th edition book Ultima Thule: Mythic Scandinavia goes into detail about Scandinavian and Norse wizards, including some stuff about Finnish practices.<br /> <br /> The 4th edition book Kabballah: Mythic Judaism covers various forms of Jewish mysticism, especially in Iberia.<br /> <br /> The 4th edition book The Dragon &amp; The Bear covers Russia and talks about Slavic, Siberian, and Mongol magic.<br /> <br /> There are four books about the Islamic world. 4th edition's Blood &amp; Sand (the Levant), and 5th edition's Between Sand and Sea (North Africa), Lands of the Nile (Egypt, Nubia, and Ethiopia), and The Cradle and The Crescent (Mesopotamia and Persia). Each talks about certain mystical traditions native to their regions.<br /> <br /> And the 5th edition book The Contested Isle covers Ireland, and has a little bit of stuff about druids and other Irish mythic traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this, Once I will have enough time and finances then I will certainly check out <i>Ars Magica books,</i> and the mentioned chapters and descriptions. I had a definite feeling that his game and setting would have some unique and particular groups, guilds, and factions.<br /> <br /> It is nice and curious to see the Amazons and citizens of Scandinavia having definite and clear representation and portrayal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T19:44:55-07:00","id":1517670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1516593#post1516593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why M20 SUCKS.<br /> <br /> I want play with the &quot;Awaken&quot;, not with the WOKE.<br /> <br /> I absolutely want my SONS of Ether to be chauvinistic arrogant a holes. I dont want politically correct idiots forged in the fires of the PC wokeist mob. I want oligarchic Hermetics and elitist VAs and authoritarian Techies. I dont want these guys to be perfectly aligned with the lgbt+ vocabulary, nor do I want them to adopt wokeist language. That's stupid, I want them to be IMPERFECT. I want them to be HUMAN.<br /> <br /> <b>They are the freaking TRADITIONS for freaking sake!!!</b>. Traditions! Not &quot;transgressives&quot;! Traditions!<br /> <br /> I dont care 2 seconds about M20. The SONS will always continue to be THE SONS of Ether on my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, what the actual fuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T05:52:33-07:00","id":1517693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CamaradaDoppio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1517670#post1517670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, what the actual fuck?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's been banned. I'm assuming for this thread, but there wasn't an official note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T08:26:30-08:00","id":1527693,"title":"","content":"I don't know why it's assumed in a mystic run world technology will remain medieval and stagnant.<br /> <br /> I can easily envision using magic to produce an advanced society. This could be a benevolent 22nd century utopia akin to the Wheel of Time's &quot;Age of Legends&quot; or a steam punk hell with fire spirits bound into train engines akin to the Chaos Dwarfs of Warhammer Fantasy, but it's easy to do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 01-03-2024, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T16:09:00-08:00","id":1528131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control#post1516384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This right here is a thought I had while I was discussing, if it weren't for Technocracy being an antagonist to the traditions, there's a possibility that the traditions would be at odds with each other, at least some of them would be, more by ideology than anything else, I could be wrong, but for the sake of argument let's assume that this is the case, what do you think would happen next if the traditions somehow defeated the technocracy or if one of them was a new Technocracy in fact and shaped the world to their creed, how do you think it would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have essentially nailed the origins of &quot;The Technocracy is right&quot; arguments.<br /> <br /> If you DON'T believe the Traditions are capable of living together in peace and harmony, the Technocracy is just winning the inevitable war.<br /> <br /> If the Traditions CAN and WILL live together in harmony then the Technocracy has been murdering, torturing, and brainwashing 15 year old Goth girls for centuries out of sheer religious fanaticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T17:21:40-08:00","id":1528135,"title":"","content":"If you look at the history of the Mage setting, there's been a ton of conflict between the Traditions. Recently that's largely been put on pause due to the Technocracy's domination. If the Technocracy collapsed, you'd start to see see the friction between the Traditions return. That's just a matter of human nature. Likewise if all the Traditions and supernatural beings were defeated, the Technocracy would start to eat itself because that's the nature of fascism. Both the Technocracy and Traditions are working within themselves because their enemies are perceived as worse than their allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T18:14:34-08:00","id":1528139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1528135#post1528135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at the history of the Mage setting, there's been a ton of conflict between the Traditions. Recently that's largely been put on pause due to the Technocracy's domination. If the Technocracy collapsed, you'd start to see see the friction between the Traditions return. That's just a matter of human nature. Likewise if all the Traditions and supernatural beings were defeated, the Technocracy would start to eat itself because that's the nature of fascism. Both the Technocracy and Traditions are working within themselves because their enemies are perceived as worse than their allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Traditions have been at peace for longer than any society in human history. Not just this generation but a dozen or more generations before it have grown up with the Euthanatos, Celestial Choir, and more being allies than enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T06:34:51-08:00","id":1528151,"title":"","content":"It's also something pointed out in <b>Guide to the Traditions</b>: while they <i>started out </i>as a highly fractious lot, the Traditions have cultivated a \u201cprinciple of harmony\u201d over the centuries, and are now the primary proponents of the notion that all kinds of Magick are just different flavorings of the same thing. This gives them common ground that the disparate factions lack, while similarly avoiding the conformity that the Technocracy imposes through its Conditioning. <br /> <br /> At least, that's the Traditional narrative. What hasn't been tested is what happens when and if the Union is taken out of the picture. Do the Traditions continue to uphold their harmonic ideal? Or do they gradually fall back into petty squabbling? If the latter, does that eventually turn into a power struggle among the Traditions, with the possibility of one emerging as the dominant force? <br /> <br /> There are those who argue that the whole \u201cwe're all doing the same thing\u201d notion is an invention of the Order of Hermes, and that accepting that premise is essentially subsuming the other Traditions under the Hermetics; that what's needed is for each Tradition to seek out its own authentic truth and to go its own way. Such attitudes are very similar to the views held by the bulk of the Disparates, which is why in my version of the setting they're a minority view among the Traditions; I like to keep the Traditions and the Disparates distinct from each other. <br /> <br /> But I could definitely see a possible future where the Traditions slowly fall apart, and eventually they all end up joining the Disparates. That wouldn't be \u201cthe Tradition in control\u201d, which is what this thread is supposed to be about; but it would certainly enhance the possibility of one (former) Tradition gaining dominance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T10:27:55-08:00","id":1532172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1517194#post1517194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Thanatoic dominated world would be potentially interesting, at least from a story perspective. Everyone is perpetually reincarnating as they slowly work their way toward their potential fated destiny. And the biggest obstacle to doing that is the personal guilt, pain, and other karmic damage one might build up during their lifetime, which will weigh them down in their next incarnation, taking them that much further from their destiny. So the upper ranks of society all around the globe are going to be a class of psychopomps whose sacred duty is to help guide others through any existing trauma so that they can continue to advance. I'm not sure how good of an RPG setting you can make out of that, but it would certainly offer an interesting setting for fiction. Stuff in the vein of Quantum Leap (at least the original; I've not seen any of the remake), the K-drama Tomorrow (about a group tasked by Heaven to prevent suicides), or maybe Person of Interest (just with fate magic instead of super computers).</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't need much for imagining a Thanatoic world.<br /> <br /> We just need to look at the Caste system of India.<br /> <br /> Perhaps also the Aztec society with their countless human sacrifices would also be a good blueprint.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it would be hell.<br /> <br /> But all for the &quot;greater good&quot;. Funny how the idea of the &quot;greater good&quot; is also the same justification of the Technocracy - or of any other tyranny for the matter. Always for the &quot;Greater Good&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T11:46:28-08:00","id":1532176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516384-the-tradition-in-control?p=1528131#post1528131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have essentially nailed the origins of &quot;The Technocracy is right&quot; arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy is right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you DON'T believe the Traditions are capable of living together in peace and harmony, the Technocracy is just winning the inevitable war.<br /> <br /> If the Traditions CAN and WILL live together in harmony then the Technocracy has been murdering, torturing, and brainwashing 15 year old Goth girls for centuries out of sheer religious fanaticism. </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy IS right, and the Traditions CANNOT live together, let alone in harmony.<br /> <br /> Let's remember that wars of extermination were not invented by the Techies, let's remember that the Eutanathoi and the Akashics tried to utterly exterminate one another - the fact that they both failed doesn't mean that they didn't want to.<br /> <br /> In Europe, let's remember that the big Hermetic project of bringing all the weirdos together into one &quot;big and happy family&quot; only happened as a consequence of their butts being kicked so hard that they were no longer taking it, but that before this, Hermetics, Verbena and Choristers were peacefully slaughtering each other.<br /> <br /> Could the US and the USSR cohexist? Sure they could... As long as they were fighting the Nazis that were hell-bent on exterminating EVERYBODY. And after that, they managed to cohexist because both had tons of nukes pointing at each other.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Technocracy is right AND they have being murdering, torturing and brainwashing AND they are religious fanatics.<br /> <br /> Mages are major A-holes. That's the beauty of it. Vampires are monsters, sure, but that's not of their own will, they are victims of circumstances imposed on them.<br /> <br /> Mages on the other hand are just major A-holes. Imagine if you could bend reality to your will, meaning that the rules that apply to everybody else do not apply to you. At the same time, you are above the pleb; you're not one of the Sleepers, you are not just another ignorant member of the masses; you are elite, you are one of the awaken, one of the select few who knows the higher truths of the cosmos that are above and beyond just simply raising kids and paying taxes.<br /> <br /> Imagine being one of these people and NOT being a massive Dick. It's almost impossible, because any &quot;normies&quot; opinions will literally be idiotic ramblings to you.<br /> <br /> In the real world, I loath anyone with a &quot;savior complex&quot; who believe themselves more knowledgeable about what's good for other better than themselves - but in the case of Mages, that would LITERALLY be true!<br /> <br /> So, in a word dominated by, I don't know, the Choristers for example, a peasant begging for food and being declined - that would ACTUALLY be better for the peasant! Because starvation would LITERALLY help him to become more enlightened!<br /> <br /> Can suffering be a route to personal growth? Sure it can. Therefore, we wouldn't be able to morally judge a Thanatoic terrorizing a village! Because, in the end, HE KNOWS BETTER!<br /> <br /> So yes, the Technocracy is right, but so are the Traditions - and they are ALL TYRANTS.<br /> <br /> I think very little people take themselves the trouble of looking at a mirror and see their own inner tyrants. I expect that everybody likes to think &quot;if I were the president/emperor/supreme-leader things would be different&quot;, and that's how EVERY SINGLE TYRANT IN HISTORY thinks!<br /> <br /> That is one of the reason why I love Mage so much: everybody who plays it see themselves as the heroes of their own stories, but they don't really realize how they are just simply tyrants imposing their wills at the end of the day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}